       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and a single dose is usually capped at 800 mg. This order is twice the daily maximum and twice the maximum single dose. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), for analgesia\n- **1600 mg/day total**, if that was the intended daily amount, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you want, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably flag it."
